  s3 --> s2: something kills the command
  s3 --> s5: the command makes its folders
  s5 --> s1: starting TLC fails
  s5 --> s2: something kills the command
  s5 --> s6: the command starts TLC
  s6 --> s1: the janitor is gone
  s6 --> s2: something kills the command
  s6 --> s7: the command tells the janitor
  s7 --> s2: something kills the command
  s7 --> s8: TLC ends or the command stops TLC
  s8 --> s2: something kills the command
  s8 --> s1: TLC failed or you pressed Ctrl-C
  s8 --> s9: TLC passed or found a bug
  s9 --> s2: something kills the command
  s9 --> s10: the check passed or found a bug
  s10 --> s1: the report prints
  s10 --> s2: something kills the command
